{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Kula","html":"<article id='thag1.19'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.19 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.19 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dutiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Two </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kulattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Kula </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Udakañhi nayanti nettikā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>While irrigators guide water, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Usukārā namayanti tejanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fletchers bend arrows straight, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dāruṁ namayanti tacchakā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and carpenters bend timber straight, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Attānaṁ damayanti subbatā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>those true to their vows tame themselves. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Kulo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
